w good components, but it doesn't feel as easy to use and natural as the other features.\nPlease make a thorough assessment of the time tracking functionality: what's good, what's bad, functionally, visually, etc.\nWrite the assessment to the docs/ folder in the workspace.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/brief.md","text":"# Brief: assessment: time tracking\n\ntype: chore\nid: whom\nbranch: chore/whom_assessment-time-tracking\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nI think the Time Tracking functionality is the weakest out of all of solytos features.\nIt is visually confusing and inconsistent. The data model doesn't feel intuitive (the way you add projects, categories, entries, etc.). The way you navigate doesn't feel intuitive.\nIt has a few good components, but it doesn't feel as easy to use and natural as the other features.\nPlease make a thorough assessment of the time tracking functionality: what's good, what's bad, functionally, visually, etc.\nWrite the assessment to the docs/ folder in the workspace.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":27,"totalLines":27,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/brief.md","time":{"start":1791627102359,"end":1791627102366}},"id":"prt_1254c0839001Y7uzSaDmQ4GDT3","sessionID":"ses_edab4348cffevuzlKCe1ty7344","messageID":"msg_1254c0071001dZ8mtcX2GAqZtf"}}
