 in the nav, delete affordances (project delete confirms on the detail page via `ConfirmationModal` but is immediate/unconfirmed in the nav sidebar; category delete is immediate; entry delete is immediate), and where editing is and is not available (entries are editable from the Entries list but not from the dashboard \"recent entries\" or the project-detail page, whose `Entry` only shows delete). Note validation gaps (e.g. save silently no-ops when duration is 0 / no project) and the default-to-first-project behaviour in `TimerWidget`/`EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit`.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/GroupedEntries.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n     depends: TASK-2\n     risk: low — concrete, file-by-file flow walkthrough\n\nTASK-4: Audit the timer, dashboard, and statistics surfaces: the start/stop timer (`TimerWidget`, `ActiveTimer`), the client-only `PomodoroWidget` (a fourth timer concept that is not persisted and does not create or link to a time entry — inconsistent with the feature's purpose), the `DashboardView` composition (Timer, Pomodoro, Today, This-Week widgets plus recent entries plus full statistics all stacked on one page), `TimeBreakdownWidget`'s project grouping (uses first category color, falls back to hardcoded `#9ca3af`), `StatisticsView` (embedded in the dashboard rather than its own tab/route; category filter filters *projects* by their categories; raw `<input type=\"date\">` with bespoke styling), and the dashboard-shell `TimeTrackingWidget` (duplicates the week-breakdown grouping logic from `DashboardView`). Assess whether timer state is honest (single active timer derived from `entries.find(stopped_at === null)`) and whether the dashboard answers the questions a user actually has.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimerWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ActiveTimer.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/PomodoroWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget.svelte\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — read-only behavioural audit of self-contained widgets\n\nTASK-5: Audit visual and interaction consistency, and compare the feature's look-and-feel against sibling features and the shared UI kit: use of shared `forms/` controls vs. hand-rolled raw inputs (e.g. `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` duration and date inputs and `TimerWidget`'s description input vs. `TextInput`; `StatisticsView` date inputs), heading/spacing conventions, hover-only affordances (`group-hover` edit/delete in the nav) and touch/Mobile usability, color handling (hardcoded hex fallbacks `#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af` across components), accessibility concerns (double-click-to-rename category, hover-revealed controls, icon-only buttons, color contrast of category chips), and i18n (unused keys such as `add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`, and the unused `pomodoro_tip` feature-tip; verify all four locales stay in sync). This is the \"visually confusing and inconsistent\" part of the brief.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/i18n/en.ts; src/lib/i18n/de.ts; src/lib/i18n/es.ts; src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — design/consistency judgement; findings must stay evidence-based (cite component + line) rather than subjective\n\nTASK-6: Write `assessment.md` in the job directory, synthesising TASK-1–5 into a single, coherent, evidence-based report: an executive summary with the headline verdict on what's good and what's broken; sections for information architecture/navigation, data model, CRUD/edit flows, timer/dashboard/statistics, and visual/consistency + accessibility/i18n; per issue, the concrete file/line reference and a suggested direction (not code); and a prioritised list of recommended follow-up changes (ranked, with effort/impact noted) so a future implementation job can pick them up. Explicitly state that no source files were changed (assessment-only), consistent with the brief and the `drama` precedent. Re-read the final document once for factual accuracy against the code before finishing.\n     files: docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n     risk: low — documentation-only deliverable\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- **Deliverable location:** the brief says \"the docs/ folder in the workspace\". There is no established top-level `docs/assessments/` convention; the closest precedent (`docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md`) places `assessment.md` inside the job directory. TASK-6 uses that location. If the author wanted a different top-level path (e.g. `docs/time-tracking-assessment.md`), that is a one-line change to TASK-6 — flag it in the implementation notes rather than guessing silently.\n- **No source changes.** Per the brief this is an assessment, not a refactor; implementations of any recommendation are out of scope and should become separate jobs.\n- **No render report / screenshots exist for this job** (checked `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/screenshots/`), so the visual claims must be grounded in the component/template source, not in rendered screenshots.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":65,"totalLines":65,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791627166221,"end":1791627166231}},"id":"prt_1254d01af001Rg0t68rCvdyMsP","sessionID":"ses_edab4348cffevuzlKCe1ty7344","messageID":"msg_1254cc93f001uVuaOWkD1Msajn"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791627166320,"sessionID":"ses_edab4348cffevuzlKCe1ty7344","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_zMxGNPNA0U92p7EyY2SQ7311","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/sheet_mobile-notifications/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/sheet_mobile-notifications/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: mobile notifications\n2: \n3: id: sheet\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\n6: date: 2026-09-12\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Task breakdown\n11: \n12: TASK-1: Create the `/notifications` route page — on mount `await load()` then `await markAllRead()` (desktop tray parity, decided: mark-all-read-on-open, not per-item), render `Entry` rows with a no-op `onClose`, header via `SubHeading` with `ts.get.nav.notifications`, and an empty-state hint `ts.get.nav.notifications_empty` shown when the list is empty (never silently dead like the desktop tray); add the new `notifications_empty` key to the `NavigationRecords` type and to the `nav` section of all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`).\n13:      files: src/routes/notifications/+page.svelte (new), src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n14:      depends: none\n15:      risk: medium — new route plus async load→markAllRead sequencing for the dots-flash effect; i18n type change forces all four files to stay in sync (`npm run check` enforces). Note: `MobileNavbar` also calls `load()` on mount, so the page should guard with `if (!userNotifications.loaded)` to avoid a duplicate fetch and an orphaned `visibilitychange` listener (the store keeps only the latest handler reference; `destroy()` removes only that one).\n16: \n17: TASK-2: Add the \"Notifications\" bell row to the mobile ⋯ overflow menu as a hardcoded entry next to settings/profile (same pattern as the settings row: `NavEntry` + `NavEntryIcon`, NOT added to `navItems`/`desktopOrder` so `getPageFeature()` and the desktop sidebar stay untouched), add `'notifications'` → lucide `bell` to the `NavEntryIcon` mapping, add `notifications: '/notifications'` to `urls.ts`, extend `overflowOnlyItems` with `notifications` for the overflow active-state mechanism, add a red dot on the ⋯ button when `getUnread().length > 0` (desktop Badge precedent uses `bg-c-btn-hover`), add an unread-count badge on the bell row (wrap in a `relative` container — `NavEntry`'s anchor is not positioned), and start the polling lifecycle in `MobileNavbar` (`onMount(() => userNotifications.load())`, `onDestroy(() => userNotifications.destroy())`).\n18:      files: src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte, src/lib/components/ui/NavEntryIcon.svelte, src/lib/config/urls.ts\n19:      depends: TASK-1 (the bell row links to the `/notifications` page)\n20:      risk: medium — modifies the overflow-menu active-state logic and adds an app-wide polling lifecycle to a persistent layout component; the badge needs a positioned wrapper inside the `NavEntry` anchor.\n21: \n22: TASK-3: Add `max-h-[calc(100dvh-8rem)] overflow-y-auto` to the ⋯ overflow menu container (the absolute `w-16` column in `MobileNavbar.svelte`) so the menu scrolls instead of overflowing/clipping on short phones (~568px); required before the 11th row (bell) lands.\n23:      files: src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte\n24:      depends: none (independent; should land before or with TASK-2)\n25:      risk: low — CSS-only change on the popup container; no menu logic touched.\n26: \n27: TASK-4: Polish `Entry.svelte` (optional per brief, small and safe): make `onClose` optional with a no-op default and render a plain non-anchor row when `notification.link` is null so mobile taps don't trigger a dead `#` link that scrolls the page; keep the `<a>` when a link exists. Desktop tray behavior is preserved because clicking still fires `goTo()` → `onClose`.\n28:      files: src/lib/components/ui/user-notifications/Entry.svelte\n29:      depends: TASK-1 (the page passes a no-op `onClose`, which the optional prop supports)\n30:      risk: low — small component change in one file; must not regress the desktop tray's click-to-close.\n31: \n32: Out of scope (do not schedule): desktop bell/navbar changes, bottom-sheet/toast notification center, per-item read/swipe-dismiss/pull-to-refresh, push-notification wiring, and the service-worker `notificationclick` no-link fallback at `/notifications` (nice-to-have, not in scope per brief). No store changes needed — `UserNotifications.svelte.ts` already provides `load()`/`destroy()`/`getUnread()`/`markAllRead()` and is context-globally available.\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: mobile notifications\n\nid: sheet\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-09-12\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Create the `/notifications` route page — on mount `await load()` then `await markAllRead()` (desktop tray parity, decided: mark-all-read-on-open, not per-item), render `Entry` rows with a no-op `onClose`, header via `SubHeading` with `ts.get.nav.notifications`, and an empty-state hint `ts.get.nav.notifications_empty` shown when the list is empty (never silently dead like the desktop tray); add the new `notifications_empty` key to the `NavigationRecords` type and to the `nav` section of all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`).\n     files: src/routes/notifications/+page.svelte (new), src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — new route plus async load→markAllRead sequencing for the dots-flash effect; i18n type change forces all four files to stay in sync (`npm run check` enforces). Note: `MobileNavbar` also calls `load()` on mount, so the page should guard with `if (!userNotifications.loaded)` to avoid a duplicate fetch and an orphaned `visibilitychange` listener (the store keeps only the latest handler reference; `destroy()` removes only that one).\n\nTASK-2: Add the \"Notifications\" bell row to the mobile ⋯ overflow menu as a hardcoded entry next to settings/profile (same pattern as the settings row: `NavEntry` + `NavEntryIcon`, NOT added to `navItems`/`desktopOrder` so `getPageFeature()` and the desktop sidebar stay untouched), add `'notifications'` → lucide `bell` to the `NavEntryIcon` mapping, add `notifications: '/notifications'` to `urls.ts`, extend `overflowOnlyItems` with `notifications` for the overflow active-state mechanism, add a red dot on the ⋯ button when `getUnread().length > 0` (desktop Badge precedent uses `bg-c-btn-hover`), add an unread-count badge on the bell row (wrap in a `relative` container — `NavEntry`'s anchor is not positioned), and start the polling lifecycle in `MobileNavbar` (`onMount(() => userNotifications.load())`, `onDestroy(() => userNotifications.destroy())`).\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte, src/lib/components/ui/NavEntryIcon.svelte, src/lib/config/urls.ts\n     depends: TASK-1 (the bell row links to the `/notifications` page)\n     risk: medium — modifies the overflow-menu active-state logic and adds an app-wide polling lifecycle to a persistent layout component; the badge needs a positioned wrapper inside the `NavEntry` anchor.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/sheet_mobile-notifications/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: mobile notifications\n\nid: sheet\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-09-12\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Create the `/notifications` route page — on mount `await load()` then `await markAllRead()` (desktop tray parity, decided: mark-all-read-on-open, not per-item), render `Entry` rows with a no-op `onClose`, header via `SubHeading` with `ts.get.nav.notifications`, and an empty-state hint `ts.get.nav.notifications_empty` shown when the list is empty (never silently dead like the desktop tray); add the new `notifications_empty` key to the `NavigationRecords` type and to the `nav` section of all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`).\n     files: src/routes/notifications/+page.svelte (new), src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — new route plus async load→markAllRead sequencing for the dots-flash effect; i18n type change forces all four files to stay in sync (`npm run check` enforces). Note: `MobileNavbar` also calls `load()` on mount, so the page should guard with `if (!userNotifications.loaded)` to avoid a duplicate fetch and an orphaned `visibilitychange` listener (the store keeps only the latest handler reference; `destroy()` removes only that one).\n\nTASK-2: Add the \"Notifications\" bell row to the mobile ⋯ overflow menu as a hardcoded entry next to settings/profile (same pattern as the settings row: `NavEntry` + `NavEntryIcon`, NOT added to `navItems`/`desktopOrder` so `getPageFeature()` and the desktop sidebar stay untouched), add `'notifications'` → lucide `bell` to the `NavEntryIcon` mapping, add `notifications: '/notifications'` to `urls.ts`, extend `overflowOnlyItems` with `notifications` for the overflow active-state mechanism, add a red dot on the ⋯ button when `getUnread().length > 0` (desktop Badge precedent uses `bg-c-btn-hover`), add an unread-count badge on the bell row (wrap in a `relative` container — `NavEntry`'s anchor is not positioned), and start the polling lifecycle in `MobileNavbar` (`onMount(() => userNotifications.load())`, `onDestroy(() => userNotifications.destroy())`).\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte, src/lib/components/ui/NavEntryIcon.svelte, src/lib/config/urls.ts\n     depends: TASK-1 (the bell row links to the `/notifications` page)\n     risk: medium — modifies the overflow-menu active-state logic and adds an app-wide polling lifecycle to a persistent layout component; the badge needs a positioned wrapper inside the `NavEntry` anchor.\n\nTASK-3: Add `max-h-[calc(100dvh-8rem)] overflow-y-auto` to the ⋯ overflow menu container (the absolute `w-16` column in `MobileNavbar.svelte`) so the menu scrolls instead of overflowing/clipping on short phones (~568px); required before the 11th row (bell) lands.\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte\n     depends: none (independent; should land before or with TASK-2)\n     risk: low — CSS-only change on the popup container; no menu logic touched.\n\nTASK-4: Polish `Entry.svelte` (optional per brief, small and safe): make `onClose` optional with a no-op default and render a plain non-anchor row when `notification.link` is null so mobile taps don't trigger a dead `#` link that scrolls the page; keep the `<a>` when a link exists. Desktop tray behavior is preserved because clicking still fires `goTo()` → `onClose`.\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/user-notifications/Entry.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1 (the page passes a no-op `onClose`, which the optional prop supports)\n     risk: low — small component change in one file; must not regress the desktop tray's click-to-close.\n\nOut of scope (do not schedule): desktop bell/navbar changes, bottom-sheet/toast notification center, per-item read/swipe-dismiss/pull-to-refresh, push-notification wiring, and the service-worker `notificationclick` no-link fallback at `/notifications` (nice-to-have, not in scope per brief). No store changes needed — `UserNotifications.svelte.ts` already provides `load()`/`destroy()`/`getUnread()`/`markAllRead()` and is context-globally available.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":32,"totalLines":32,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/sheet_mobile-notifications/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791627166314,"end":1791627166318}},"id":"prt_1254d020f001B4Xl87MMwRc1Sr"