{"type":"text","timestamp":1791627189765,"sessionID":"ses_edab4348cffevuzlKCe1ty7344","part":{"id":"prt_1254d5504001JdlDhM49nQlhu0","messageID":"msg_1254d4cb0001VvW6EK5aYFWBpG","sessionID":"ses_edab4348cffevuzlKCe1ty7344","type":"text","text":"I've read the brief, the archived assessment it references, and the time-tracking source, and written the task list to `docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/tasks.md`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**18 tasks**, sequenced foundation-first as the brief requires:\n\n- **TASK-1–3 — contract mirror + navigation:** update `types/time_tracking.ts` to the post-change contract (optional project `color`, editable `has_exact_times` on update, statistics category param); make the Dashboard/Entries view URL-driven; replace the sidebar's inline `display` toggle with the `open`-state + `fly` drawer pattern.\n- **TASK-4–5 — single source of truth:** extract a pure, unit-tested grouping/colour service (removing both duplicated `groupByProject` copies and the `uncategorized` fallback), and consume `total_duration`/statistics instead of hand-reduced totals.\n- **TASK-6–9 — unified entry CRUD:** merge `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit`, fix backdating/date semantics, stop defaulting to `projects[0]`, make entries editable on every surface.\n- **TASK-10–12 — dashboard/statistics:** separate working surface from analytics, resolve the Pomodoro, make statistics consistent (colour source, date/unit convention, local-time defaults, real category filter).\n- **TASK-13–14 — destructive actions + discoverability/a11y.**\n- **TASK-15–18 — polish:** reuse the existing `NumberInput`/`DateInput`, validation feedback, contrast/hex-literal cleanup, dead i18n keys, heading/spacing.\n\n**Two things you should know (flagged in the file, not blocking the list):**\n\n1. **`docs/tt-assessment.md` does not exist at that path.** The assessment the brief calls its line-level authority is at `docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md` — I mapped its §6 items 1–15 to the tasks.\n2. **`api-brief.md` is not present anywhere in the repo.** I did *not* stop: the brief itself enumerates the required contract changes (editable `has_exact_times`, project `color`, authoritative `total_duration`, cascade contract, category-filterable statistics), so a conservative breakdown is possible. But the **exact field/parameter names are unverified** — this is the main scope risk and is called out for TASK-1/TASK-12.\n\nAlso noted: `NumberInput`/`DateInput` already exist in `forms/` (the assessment predates them), and `TASK-11` (Pomodoro wire-up vs move-out) is a genuine product decision the brief leaves open.\n\nI did not commit `tasks.md` (read-only), and could not execute `git` in this session; the worktree gitdir (`.../.git/worktrees/joke_time-tracking-improvements`) matches the job's branch context.","time":{"start":1791627187460,"end":1791627189763}}}
