{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791627194120,"sessionID":"ses_edab29d7fffe7q7IOFDa3tpcmo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_TxWYS9RyTkkzrVXWDOJo3166","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: time tracking improvements\n2: \n3: type: feature\n4: id: joke\n5: branch: feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements\n6: date: 2026-10-10\n7: author: Leander Muskalla\n8: \n9: ## What\n10: \n11: Rework time tracking so its UI stops hiding, duplicating, and contradicting the\n12: data model it already has. The domain model is sound (projects own many\n13: categories; a single running timer derived from entries), and the store/contract\n14: layer plus `ActiveTimer` are solid — keep them. This job addresses the full set\n15: of findings in `docs/tt-assessment.md` (its §6 table is the line-level\n16: authority): navigation and information architecture, the create/edit flows,\n17: dashboard and statistics composition, and visual/accessibility/i18n consistency.\n18: The assessment changed no source; this is the follow-up implementation.\n19: \n20: Notable changes, grouped as workstreams:\n21: \n22: - **URL-driven navigation.** Move the Dashboard/Entries view (and ideally the\n23:   selected project) into the route or a search param so reload, deep-linking, and\n24:   back/forward restore the view; derive the active tab from the URL instead of\n25:   store state. Replace the sidebar's inline `display` toggle with the app's\n26:   `open`-state + transition drawer pattern used by todos/notes.\n27: - **Discoverable management.** Stop hiding project/category actions behind hover\n28:   and double-click; give icon-only buttons accessible names and make the same\n29:   actions reachable by touch and keyboard.\n30: - **Single source of truth for durations and colours.** Consume\n31:   `project.total_duration` and/or the statistics endpoint instead of recomputing\n32:   totals by hand; remove the duplicated `groupByProject` (including the\n33:   dashboard-shell widget's copy); colour each project from its own `color` field\n34:   (added per `api-brief.md`), never from its first category; replace the\n35:   `#1dbda5`/`#888`/`#9ca3af` literals with theme variables.\n36: - **Correct domain semantics.** Fix backdating so a duration-only entry anchors\n37:   to a defined time and lands on the day the user chose (never rolling into the\n38:   previous day); make the date field meaningful or hidden when exact times are\n39:   used; send `has_exact_times` on both create and update (the update field is\n40:   added per `api-brief.md`) and rely on the clarified anchor rule for\n41:   duration-only entries; assume the cascade contract (entries are deleted with\n42:   their project, per `api-brief.md`) and drop the `uncategorized` fallback in\n43:   the breakdown widgets; and stop silently defaulting entries/timers to\n44:   `tt.projects[0]`.\n45: - **Unified entry CRUD.** Replace `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` with one component\n46:   (optional editing entry) that sends consistent timestamps and exposes a real\n47:   date control, and make entries editable from every surface that shows them\n48:   (dashboard recent entries, project detail, entries tab).\n49: - **Dashboard and statistics.** Separate the working surface (timer, entries)\n50:   from analytics; move or repurpose the unintegrated Pomodoro so it no longer\n51:   competes with the real timer; and make statistics consistent — one project\n52:   colour source, one date/unit convention, a local-time default range, and a\n53:   category filter that uses the statistics endpoint's category param (added per\n54:   `api-brief.md`) so it filters entries by category rather than silently\n55:   restricting projects.\n56: - **Safe destructive actions.** Confirm or offer undo for project, category, and\n57:   entry deletes everywhere (detail page and sidebar must behave the same).\n58: - **Consistency, a11y, i18n.** Reuse shared form controls (or add\n59:   `NumberInput`/`DateInput` in the existing `forms/` layer) for number, date, and\n60:   timer inputs; guard category-chip contrast; add explicit validation feedback\n61:   instead of silent no-ops; associate labels with inputs; remove or wire up the\n62:   six unused `timeTracking` keys and the orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking`\n63:   tips across all four locales; normalise headings and spacing via the shared\n64:   `Heading` component.\n65: \n66: ## Why\n67: \n68: Time tracking is solyto's least usable feature: its navigation, data model, and\n69: CRUD flows are hidden, duplicated, or inconsistent with the rest of the app, so\n70: users cannot reliably add, find, edit, or trust their tracked time.\n71: \n72: ## Out of scope\n73: \n74: - **Backend/API changes.** This repo consumes a REST API owned elsewhere, so a\n75:   frontend job cannot add server fields or endpoints. The contract changes this\n76:   job needs are tracked in `api-brief.md` and are assumed to land: an editable\n77:   `has_exact_times` on the update payload, a first-class project `color`, an\n78:   authoritative `total_duration`, a resolved project-less/cascade contract, and\n79:   a category-filterable statistics endpoint. The frontend must consume the\n80:   post-change contract directly — update `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` (and\n81:   `apiRoutes.ts` where relevant) to match — rather than falling back to\n82:   frontend-only approximations. If a required change is missing on the API or\n83:   consuming it would break something on the frontend, stop and flag it; do not\n84:   invent a workaround.\n85: - **Rewriting the store/contract layer or `ActiveTimer`** — both are sound\n86:   foundations (assessment §\"What works well\"); a rewrite would add risk without\n87:   fixing any reported problem.\n88: - **Redesigning the app-wide visual language.** The brief is about time tracking\n89:   feeling inconsistent *with the rest of the app*; changing the app-wide language\n90:   would move the inconsistency rather than resolve it. Shared-component additions\n91:   are allowed only if they do not alter other features' behaviour.\n92: - **Net-new product features** (recurring entries, new reporting, etc.) — this job\n93:   makes the existing model usable and coherent; new capability is a separate\n94:   decision.\n95: \n96: ## Notes\n97: \n98: - The API changes in `api-brief.md` are assumed to be fulfilled alongside this\n99:   job; do not code against the current contract's gaps (e.g. the un-editable\n100:   `has_exact_times`, the missing project `color`) as if they were permanent.\n101: - Frontend-only repo: `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` and\n102:   `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts` mirror the API contract. Update the type mirrors\n103:   to the post-change contract (all new fields optional/backward-compatible) in\n104:   the same job that consumes them.\n105: - Every claim in `docs/tt-assessment.md` is already verified to `file:line`; use\n106:   its §6 table as the checklist and the body for detail.\n107: - Follow existing patterns: one runes store per domain, pure logic extracted to\n108:   `src/lib/services/` and unit-tested (see `TodoGroupingService`), shared\n109:   controls in `src/lib/components/forms/`.\n110: - Keep all four i18n locales in sync and update the shared type when removing\n111:   keys — `npm run check` enforces both.\n112: - This is intentionally one large job with distinct workstreams: land the\n113:   foundation (navigation, data model, unified CRUD) before the polish. If a\n114:   workstream balloons, flag it rather than silently expanding scope.\n115: - Verify with `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm test`; add unit tests for\n116:   any extracted grouping/duration/colour logic (this repo has no component\n117:   tests).\n118: - Preserve the parts the assessment called out as good: the store's parallel\n119:   load-and-reload, the single-timer-derived-from-entries model, and the honest\n120:   `ActiveTimer`.\n\n(End of file - total 120 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: time tracking improvements\n\ntype: feature\nid: joke\nbranch: feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRework time tracking so its UI stops hiding, duplicating, and contradicting the\ndata model it already has. The domain model is sound (projects own many\ncategories; a single running timer derived from entries), and the store/contract\nlayer plus `ActiveTimer` are solid — keep them. This job addresses the full set\nof findings in `docs/tt-assessment.md` (its §6 table is the line-level\nauthority): navigation and information architecture, the create/edit flows,\ndashboard and statistics composition, and visual/accessibility/i18n consistency.\nThe assessment changed no source; this is the follow-up implementation.\n\nNotable changes, grouped as workstreams:","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/brief.md","text":"# Brief: time tracking improvements\n\ntype: feature\nid: joke\nbranch: feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRework time tracking so its UI stops hiding, duplicating, and contradicting the\ndata model it already has. The domain model is sound (projects own many\ncategories; a single running timer derived from entries), and the store/contract\nlayer plus `ActiveTimer` are solid — keep them. This job addresses the full set\nof findings in `docs/tt-assessment.md` (its §6 table is the line-level\nauthority): navigation and information architecture, the create/edit flows,\ndashboard and statistics composition, and visual/accessibility/i18n consistency.\nThe assessment changed no source; this is the follow-up implementation.\n\nNotable changes, grouped as workstreams:\n\n- **URL-driven navigation.** Move the Dashboard/Entries view (and ideally the\n  selected project) into the route or a search param so reload, deep-linking, and\n  back/forward restore the view; derive the active tab from the URL instead of\n  store state. Replace the sidebar's inline `display` toggle with the app's\n  `open`-state + transition drawer pattern used by todos/notes.\n- **Discoverable management.** Stop hiding project/category actions behind hover\n  and double-click; give icon-only buttons accessible names and make the same\n  actions reachable by touch and keyboard.\n- **Single source of truth for durations and colours.** Consume\n  `pr