e hard-coded colour literals (`#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af`) with theme variables across the feature.\n106:      files: src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; the TASK-4 service and its consumers\n107:      depends: TASK-4 (colour logic centralised)\n108:      risk: low — styling/contrast only, but needs a readable-text rule for light category colours.\n109: \n110: TASK-17: Remove (or wire up) the six unused `timeTracking` keys (`add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`) and the orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking` tips across all four locales, updating the shared `TimeTrackingRecords` type — keys being removed must be dropped from `src/lib/types/translation.ts` or `npm run check` fails.\n111:      files: src/lib/i18n/en.ts; src/lib/i18n/de.ts; src/lib/i18n/es.ts; src/lib/i18n/fr.ts; src/lib/types/translation.ts\n112:      depends: none\n113:      risk: low — but every key must be genuinely unreferenced (note `add_category` also exists in other i18n sections at line 234; only remove the `timeTracking` one).\n114: \n115: TASK-18: Normalise headings and spacing via the shared `Heading` component — use it consistently for section titles on the dashboard, statistics, breakdown widget and project detail, and align the vertical rhythm between those surfaces.\n116:      files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n117:      depends: TASK-10 (dashboard composition settled)\n118:      risk: low — presentational, but `Heading` expects a numeric `my` prop.\n119: \n120: ## Source-of-truth docs (verify before starting)\n121: \n122: - **`docs/tt-assessment.md` is not present at that path.** The assessment the\n123:   brief calls its line-level authority exists at\n124:   `docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md`; its §6 table\n125:   is items 1–15 and maps to TASK-2 (1), TASK-6 (2), TASK-7 (3), TASK-4/5 (4),\n126:   TASK-11 (5), TASK-13 (6), TASK-9 (7), TASK-3 (8), TASK-14 (9), TASK-15 (10),\n127:   TASK-15 (11), TASK-4 (12), TASK-17 (13), TASK-7/12 (14), TASK-18 (15).\n128: - **`api-brief.md` is not present anywhere in the repo.** The required API\n129:   changes are enumerated only in the brief itself: an editable `has_exact_times`\n130:   on the update payload, a first-class project `color`, an authoritative\n131:   `total_duration`, a resolved project-less/cascade contract, and a\n132:   category-filterable statistics endpoint. The brief says to consume the\n133:   post-change contract directly and *not* to invent a frontend workaround. The\n134:   missing `api-brief.md` is the main scope risk (see open questions).\n135: \n136: ## Open questions / risks\n137: \n138: - **Exact API field and parameter names are unverified.** TASK-1/TASK-12 need\n139:   the real names for the project `color` field and the statistics category\n140:   parameter. The brief gives intent, not schema. Confirm against the API owner\n141:   before coding; if the API change is not actually available, stop and flag it\n142:   rather than approximating on the frontend.\n143: - **Pomodoro disposition (TASK-11) is a product decision** — wire it to a real\n144:   entry or move it out. The brief allows either; the developer should not guess.\n145:   Recommend the least-risky option (move it out of the time-tracking dashboard)\n146:   and note the choice in `implementation.md` if the author cannot confirm.\n147: - **`total_duration` semantics** (TASK-5): units, update freshness after timer\n148:   stop / entry edit, and whether it includes running entries need confirming.\n149: - **Branch:** the brief names `feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements`. This\n150:   read-only session has no shell, so the branch could not be executed; the\n151:   worktree gitdir (`.../.git/worktrees/joke_time-tracking-improvements`)\n152:   matches the job, consistent with the pipeline's per-job worktree.\n153: - **No render report / screenshots exist for this job**, so all visual claims\n154:   are grounded in component source, not rendered pixels.\n155: - **Verification for every task:** `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`;\n156:   add/extend unit tests for any extracted grouping/duration/colour logic (this\n157:   repo has no component tests). Keep all four i18n locales in sync and update\n158:   the shared type whenever keys change.\n\n(End of file - total 158 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief reworks the Time Tracking feature against `docs/tt-assessment.md`\n(§6 table = line-level authority) and assumes the API changes in\n`api-brief.md` land alongside this job. Two paths referenced by the brief are\n**not present at the stated locations**; see \"Source-of-truth docs\" below.\n\nThe store/contract layer (`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts`) and\n`ActiveTimer.svelte` are explicitly out of scope for rewriting — keep them. The\nwork is sequenced \"foundation first, polish later\": contract mirror + navigation\n(TASK-1–3), single source of truth for durations/colours (TASK-4–5), unified","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief reworks the Time Tracking feature against `docs/tt-assessment.md`\n(§6 table = line-level authority) and assumes the API changes in\n`api-brief.md` land alongside this job. Two paths referenced by the brief are\n**not present at the stated locations**; see \"Source-of-truth docs\" below.\n\nThe store/contract layer (`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts`) and\n`ActiveTimer.svelte` are explicitly out of scope for rewriting — keep them. The\nwork is sequenced \"foundation first, polish later\": contract mirror + navigation\n(TASK-1–3), single source of truth for durations/colours (TASK-4–5), unified\nentry CRUD (TASK-6–9), dashboard/statistics composition (TASK-10–12), then\ndestructive actions / discoverability / a11y (TASK-13–14) and polish (TASK-15–18).\n\nThe repository already has `src/lib/components/forms/NumberInput.svelte` and\n`DateInput.svelte` (plus `DateTimeInput.svelte`), so TASK-15 is \"reuse the\nexisting shared controls\", not \"add new ones\" (the assessment predates them).\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Update the frontend contract mirror in `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` to the post-change API shape assumed by the brief — add an optional project `color` to `TimeTrackingProject` and to `Create`/`UpdateTimeTrackingProjectRequest`, add optional `has_exact_times` to `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`, and add the statistics category-filter parameter to `TimeTrackingStatistics`/the `loadStatistics` signature — keeping every addition optional/backward-compatible so the current API keeps type-checking.\n     files: src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts (loadStatistics signature); src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts (only if the statistics route needs a param)\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the exact field/param names come from `api-brief.md`, which is not in this repo; confirm the shape before consuming it (see open questions).\n\nTASK-2: Make the Dashboard/Entries view (and ideally the selected project) URL-driven — encode the active tab in the route or a `?tab=` search param, derive `activeTab` from `page.url` instead of the store's `$state`, and give the two nav links distinct targets so reload, deep-link and back/forward restore the view; keep the active-highlight in sync with the URL.\n     files: src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/+layout.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts; src/lib/config/urls.ts\n     depends: none (touches the nav; coordinate ordering with TASK-3)\n     risk: medium — changes how the feature is entered and requires a route-or-search-param decision.\n\nTASK-3: Replace `TimeTrackingNavigation`'s inline `style.display` mobile toggle with the app's `open`-state + transition drawer pattern (as in `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` / `notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`): an `open` `$state` flag, `{#if open}` with `transition:fly`, `HamburgerButton` and `CloseButton`.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte\n     depends: TASK-2 (same file — land TASK-2 first to avoid conflicts)\n     risk: medium — the current inline `display` competes with the `lg:flex` class and provides no transition/focus handling; must not regress desktop layout.\n\nTASK-4: Extract the duplicated project grouping/colour logic into one pure, unit-tested service and use it everywhere — group entries by project using the project's own new `color` field (with a theme-variable fallback), drop the `uncategorized` fallback (entries always belong to a project), remove both `groupByProject` copies (`DashboardView` and the dashboard-shell `TimeTrackingWidget`), and add a Vitest unit test following the `TodoGroupingService` pattern.\n     files: src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts (new); tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts (new); src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1 (project `color` field)\n     risk: medium — shared logic consumed by two surfaces plus the shell widget; the unit test locks the colour/total rules.\n\nTASK-5: Consume the authoritative duration instead of recomputing totals by hand — replace the sidebar `projectDurations` reduce and the project-detail `totalDuration` reduce with `project.total_duration` (and/or the statistics endpoint), leaving one source of truth for a project's total.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — must confirm `total_duration` units/currency and that it is refreshed after entry mutations.\n\nTASK-6: Unify `EntryCreate` and `EntryEdit` into one component taking an optional editing entry — send consistent ISO timestamps from both paths, send `has_exact_times` on create **and** update, expose a real date control, and update every call site.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/GroupedEntries.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1 (update can now carry `has_exact_times`)\n     risk: high — merges two files that currently disagree on timezone handling, and touches all three surfaces that open the form.\n\nTASK-7: Fix duration-only backdating semantics in the unified entry component — anchor a duration-only entry to a defined local time so the chosen day is honoured and never rolls into the previous calendar day, derive the displayed day from that anchor, make the date field meaningful or hidden when exact times are used, and stop computing the default date via `toISOString()` (UTC).\n     files: the unified entry component from TASK-6 (currently `EntryCreate.svelte`/`EntryEdit.svelte`)\n     depends: TASK-6\n     risk: medium — subtle date/timezone behaviour that the assessment calls out as a concrete bug.\n\nTASK-8: Stop silently defaulting entries and the timer to `tt.projects[0]` — require an explicit project choice (no first-project default) in the unified entry form and in `TimerWidget`, with user-visible feedback rather than a silent no-op.\n     files: the unified entry component from TASK-6; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimerWidget.svelte\n     depends: TASK-6\n     risk: low/medium — small change but affects the common \"start a timer / add an entry\" path and could surprise repeat users.\n\nTASK-9: Make entries editable from every surface that shows them — add the edit affordance to the dashboard's recent entries and the project-detail page (the Entries tab already edits), wiring them to the unified entry component.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/GroupedEntries.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte\n     depends: TASK-6\n     risk: low/medium — presentational wiring once the component is unified.\n\nTASK-10: Separate the working surface from analytics — move the full `StatisticsView` out of the dashboard body (its own view/tab/route) so the dashboard is the timer + entries and statistics is a distinct surface.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte\n     depends: TASK-2 (view routing)\n     risk: medium — re-homes an entire panel and changes what the dashboard is.\n\nTASK-11: Give the Pomodoro a purpose or a home — either wire `PomodoroWidget` to create/link a real entry with shared timer UI, or move it out of the time-tracking dashboard so it no longer competes with the real timer.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/PomodoroWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — this is an unresolved product decision (wire-up vs move-out); do not guess, see open questions.\n\nTASK-12: Make statistics consistent — one project colour source (project `color`, not first category), one date/unit convention (drop the hours-decimal category bars in favour of the shared duration format), a local-time default range instead of `toISOString()`, and a category filter that calls the statistics endpoint's category parameter instead of silently restricting projects client-side.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts; src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — changes the filter semantics the user sees and touches the statistics request.\n\nTASK-13: Confirm or offer undo for project, category and entry deletes everywhere — route the sidebar project delete (currently immediate) and the category/entry deletes through the same confirmation/undo treatment the project-detail page already uses, so the same action behaves the same from every surface.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n     depends: none (coordinate the shared file with TASK-3/TASK-14)\n     risk: low/medium — adds a confirm step to currently-instant actions; watch for double-confirmation on the detail page.\n\nTASK-14: Make project/category management discoverable and accessible — replace hover-only project controls and double-click-to-rename with explicit affordances reachable by touch and keyboard, and give icon-only buttons accessible names; apply the same to the shared `InlineEditButton`/`InlineDeleteButton` where they hide the real button on hover.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/ui/buttons/InlineEditButton.svelte; src/lib/components/ui/buttons/InlineDeleteButton.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte\n     depends: TASK-3 (drawer structure), TASK-13 (same nav file)\n     risk: medium — shared button components are used beyond time tracking; changes must not alter other features' behaviour.\n\nTASK-15: Reuse the existing shared form controls and add explicit validation feedback — swap the raw number/date/timer inputs for `NumberInput`/`DateInput`/`TextInput`, associate labels with their inputs (`<label for>`), and replace the silent `return` guards with disabled-Save or a visible message in the entry, project and timer forms.\n     files: the unified entry component from TASK-6; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimerWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte\n     depends: TASK-6\n     risk: low — mechanical reuse of existing controls, but the shared controls' prop shapes must be matched.\n\nTASK-16: Guard category-chip contrast and replace the hard-coded colour literals (`#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af`) with theme variables across the feature.\n     files: src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; the TASK-4 service and its consumers\n     depends: TASK-4 (colour logic centralised)\n     risk: low — styling/contrast only, but needs a readable-text rule for light category colours.\n\nTASK-17: Remove (or wire up) the six unused `timeTracking` keys (`add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`) and the orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking` tips across all four locales, updating the shared `TimeTrackingRecords` type — keys being removed must be dropped from `src/lib/types/translation.ts` or `npm run check` fails.\n     files: src/lib/i18n/en.ts; src/lib/i18n/de.ts; src/lib/i18n/es.ts; src/lib/i18n/fr.ts; src/lib/types/translation.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — but every key must be genuinely unreferenced (note `add_category` also exists in other i18n sections at line 234; only remove the `timeTracking` one).\n\nTASK-18: Normalise headings and spacing via the shared `Heading` component — use it consistently for section titles on the dashboard, statistics, breakdown widget and project detail, and align the vertical rhythm between those surfaces.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n     depends: TASK-10 (dashboard composition settled)\n     risk: low — presentational, but `Heading` expects a numeric `my` prop.\n\n## Source-of-truth docs (verify before starting)\n\n- **`docs/tt-assessment.md` is not present at that path.** The assessment the\n  brief calls its line-level authority exists at\n  `docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md`; its §6 table\n  is items 1–15 and maps to TASK-2 (1), TASK-6 (2), TASK-7 (3), TASK-4/5 (4),\n  TASK-11 (5), TASK-13 (6), TASK-9 (7), TASK-3 (8), TASK-14 (9), TASK-15 (10),\n  TASK-15 (11), TASK-4 (12), TASK-17 (13), TASK-7/12 (14), TASK-18 (15).\n- **`api-brief.md` is not present anywhere in the repo.** The required API\n  changes are enumerated only in the brief itself: an editable `has_exact_times`\n  on the update payload, a first-class project `color`, an authoritative\n  `total_duration`, a resolved project-less/cascade contract, and a\n  category-filterable statistics endpoint. The brief says to consume the\n  post-change contract directly and *not* to invent a frontend workaround. The\n  missing `api-brief.md` is the main scope risk (see open questions).\n\n## Open questions / risks\n\n- **Exact API field and parameter names are unverified.** TASK-1/TASK-12 need\n  the real names for the project `color` field and the statistics category\n  parameter. The brief gives intent, not schema. Confirm against the API owner\n  before coding; if the API change is not actually available, stop and flag it\n  rather than approximating on the frontend.\n- **Pomodoro disposition (TASK-11) is a product decision** — wire it to a real\n  entry or move it out. The brief allows either; the developer should not guess.\n  Recommend the least-risky option (move it out of the time-tracking dashboard)\n  and note the choice in `implementation.md` if the author cannot confirm.\n- **`total_duration` semantics** (TASK-5): units, update freshness after timer\n  stop / entry edit, and whether it includes running entries need confirming.\n- **Branch:** the brief names `feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements`. This\n  read-only session has no shell, so the branch could not be executed; the\n  worktree gitdir (`.../.git/worktrees/joke_time-tracking-improvements`)\n  matches the job, consistent with the pipeline's per-job worktree.\n- **No render report / screenshots exist for this job**, so all visual claims\n  are grounded in component source, not rendered pixels.\n- **Verification for every task:** `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`;\n  add/extend unit tests for any extracted grouping/duration/colour logic (this\n  repo has no component tests). Keep all four i18n locales in sync and update\n  the shared type whenever keys change.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":158,"totalLines":158,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791628358216,"end":1791628358224}},"id":"prt_1255f3211001jWB0xHeVHQKxBl","sessionID":"ses_edaa0f8d5ffeDEZMADxwKw1010","messageID":"msg_1255f2cc80014amDAUTKD6bYYG"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791628358310,"sessionID":"ses_edaa0f8d5ffeDEZMADxwKw1010","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_eW68nQ5UpvO8ziI0936C6998","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: time tracking improvements\n2: \n3: id: joke\n4: developer: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: Reworked the Time Tracking feature end to end so its UI matches the domain\n10: model: URL-driven navigation, discoverable/accessible management, one source of\n11: truth for durations and colours, a single unified entry component with correct\n12: backdating, editing everywhere entries are shown, a separated statistics\n13: surface, confirmed destructive actions, shared form controls, and cleaner\n14: i18n/heading conventions. The store/contract layer and `ActiveTimer` were kept\n15: as-is (only additive contract-mirror changes).\n16: \n17: ## Changes\n18: \n19: TASK-1: Updated the contract mirror in `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` — added\n20: optional `color` to `TimeTrackingProject` and to the create/update project\n21: requests, added optional `has_exact_times` to `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`,\n22: and added a `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type. `loadStatistics` in\n23: `src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts` now takes an optional `categoryIds` array\n24: and appends it as the statistics category filter.\n25: \n26: TASK-2: Made the view URL-driven. Removed `activeTab` from the store; the active\n27: tab is derived from `?tab=` in both `src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte` and\n28: `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte`, and the nav links now have distinct targets\n29: (`/time-tracking` vs `?tab=entries`), so reload/deep-link/back-forward work.\n30: \n31: TASK-3: Replaced the sidebar's inline `style.display` toggle with the app's\n32: `open` `$state` + `{#if open}` + `transition:fly` drawer pattern (a shared\n33: `{#snippet sidebar()}` renders into both the desktop column and the mobile\n34: drawer), matching todos/notes.\n35: \n36: TASK-4: Added `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts` (pure,\n37: unit-tested) that groups entries by project using the project's own `color`\n38: (theme-variable fallback), drops the impossible `uncategorized` state, and sorts\n39: by minutes. Replaced both `groupByProject` copies (`DashboardView`,\n40: `dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget`) and typed `TimeBreakdownWidget` from the\n41: service. New test: `tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts`.\n42: \n43: TASK-5: Replaced the sidebar and project-detail duration reduces with\n44: `project.total_duration`.\n45: \n46: TASK-6/7/8 (landed together; same file): Unified `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` into\n47: one `EntryCreate.svelte` with an optional `entry` prop and deleted\n48: `EntryEdit.svelte`. Both paths send consistent ISO timestamps and\n49: `has_exact_times` on create *and* update. Duration-only entries anchor to local\n50: noon of the chosen day (never rolling into the previous day); the date field is\n51: hidden when exact times are used; default dates are local, not `toISOString()`.\n52: Removed the `tt.projects[0]` defaults from the entry form and `TimerWidget`, and\n53: both now disable Save/Start plus require an explicit project.\n54: \n55: TASK-9: Entries are now editable from the dashboard's recent entries and the\n56: project-detail page (the Entries tab already was), all wired to the unified\n57: component.\n58: \n59: TASK-10: Moved `StatisticsView` out of `DashboardView` onto its own\n60: `?tab=statistics` surface with a sidebar link.\n61: \n62: TASK-11: Removed `PomodoroWidget` from the time-tracking dashboard so it no\n63: longer competes with the real timer. The component file is left in place,\n64: currently unreferenced — see follow-ups.\n65: \n66: TASK-12: Statistics now uses the project's own colour, passes the category\n67: filter to the statistics endpoint (`category_ids`) instead of restricting\n68: projects client-side, defaults its range in local time, and reports the category\n69: bar in the shared duration format rather than hours-with-decimals.\n70: \n71: TASK-13: Routed sidebar project/category deletes and all entry deletes through\n72: `ConfirmationModal`, so the same action behaves the same from every surface\n73: (the detail page already confirmed project deletes).\n74: \n75: TASK-14: Removed the hover-only project controls (always visible now), replaced\n76: double-click-to-rename with an explicit pencil button, labelled the colour\n77: picker, and added `aria-label`s to all icon-only controls. `InlineEditButton`/\n78: `InlineDeleteButton` gained an optional `label` prop (accessible name) and\n79: `focus-visible:opacity-100`, without changing other features' behaviour.\n80: \n81: TASK-15: Reused `NumberInput`/`DateInput`/`TextInput` across the entry, timer,\n82: statistics and project forms, wrapped fields in `<label>` for implicit\n83: association, and replaced silent no-ops with disabled Save buttons (entry,\n84: timer, project).\n85: \n86: TASK-16: Added `isLightColor`/`getReadableTextColor` to `ColorHelper` (+ tests)\n87: and used it to guard category-chip/pill contrast; replaced the `#888`/`#9ca3af`\n88: literals with theme variables and centralised the category default.\n89: \n90: TASK-17: Removed the genuinely unused `timeTracking` keys `duration_minutes`,\n91: `category`, and `this_month` from all four locales and the shared type.\n92: \n93: TASK-18: Used the shared `Heading` for the dashboard title, statistics heading,\n94: breakdown-widget title and project-detail title, and spaced the dashboard with a\n95: consistent vertical rhythm.\n96: \n97: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n98: \n99: - **API contract names are assumed.** `api-brief.md` is not present anywhere in\n100:   the repo, so the post-change contract was mirrored from the brief's intent:\n101:   project `color`, update `has_exact_times`, and the statistics filter were named\n102:   `category_ids` (consistent with the project `category_ids` field). These are\n103:   all optional/backward-compatible; confirm the real names with the API owner.\n104: - **`project.total_duration` unit assumed to be minutes** (formatted with the\n105:   existing `formatDuration`, which takes minutes). Confirm the unit.\n106: - **Pomodoro (TASK-11) has no home yet.** Per the brief's \"move it out\" option it\n107:   was removed from the time-tracking dashboard; `PomodoroWidget.svelte` is now\n108:   unreferenced and awaits a product decision (wire to a real entry vs. relocate).\n109: - **TASK-17 scope reduction.** `add_category`, `edit_category`, and `color` are\n110:   now referenced by TASK-14 (the brief allows \"remove *or* wire up\"), and the\n111:   `welcome_tour.steps.timeTracking` tips are consumed by `WelcomeTour.svelte`\n112:   (the task's \"orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking`\" does not exist in the repo),\n113:   so those were kept.\n114: - **Pre-existing verification failures** (present before this job, unrelated):\n115:   `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` \"StatisticWidget\" colour-class test\n116:   fails, and `npm run lint` fails prettier across ~450 untouched files. There are\n117:   also pre-existing eslint errors in untouched files (e.g. `Calendars.svelte.ts`).\n118:   `npm run check` is clean and all time-tracking/new tests pass.\n119: - `node_modules` was absent; `npm ci` was run to restore the pinned dependencies\n120:   purely to execute the project's own `check`/`test`/`lint` commands. No\n121:   dependency was added or changed.\n\n(End of file - total 121 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n## Summary\n\nReworked the Time Tracking feature end to end so its UI matches the domain\nmodel: URL-driven navigation, discoverable/accessible management, one source of\ntruth for durations and colours, a single unified entry component with correct\nbackdating, editing everywhere entries are shown, a separated statistics\nsurface, confirmed destructive actions, shared form controls, and cleaner\ni18n/heading conventions. The store/contract layer and `ActiveTimer` were kept\nas-is (only additive contract-mirror changes).\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Updated the contract mirror in `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` — added\noptional `color` to `TimeTrackingProject` and to the create/update project","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n## Summary\n\nReworked the Time Tracking feature end to end so its UI matches the domain\nmodel: URL-driven navigation, discoverable/accessible management, one source of\ntruth for durations and colours, a single unified entry component with correct\nbackdating, editing everywhere entries are shown, a separated statistics\nsurface, confirmed destructive actions, shared form controls, and cleaner\ni18n/heading conventions. The store/contract layer and `ActiveTimer` were kept\nas-is (only additive contract-mirror changes).\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Updated the contract mirror in `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` — added\noptional `color` to `TimeTrackingProject` and to the create/update project\nrequests, added optional `has_exact_times` to `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`,\nand added a `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type. `loadStatistics` in\n`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts` now takes an optional `categoryIds` array\nand appends it as the statistics category filter.\n\nTASK-2: Made the view URL-driven. Removed `activeTab` from the store; the active\ntab is derived from `?tab=` in both `src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte` and\n`TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte`, and the nav links now have distinct targets\n(`/time-tracking` vs `?tab=entries`), so reload/deep-link/back-forward work.\n\nTASK-3: Replaced the sidebar's inline `style.display` toggle with the app's\n`open` `$state` + `{#if open}` + `transition:fly` drawer pattern (a shared\n`{#snippet sidebar()}` renders into both the desktop column and the mobile\ndrawer), matching todos/notes.\n\nTASK-4: Added `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts` (pure,\nunit-tested) that groups entries by project using the project's own `color`\n(theme-variable fallback), drops the impossible `uncategorized` state, and sorts\nby minutes. Replaced both `groupByProject` copies (`DashboardView`,\n`dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget`) and typed `TimeBreakdownWidget` from the\nservice. New test: `tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts`.\n\nTASK-5: Replaced the sidebar and project-detail duration reduces with\n`project.total_duration`.\n\nTASK-6/7/8 (landed together; same file): Unified `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` into\none `EntryCreate.svelte` with an optional `entry` prop and deleted\n`EntryEdit.svelte`. Both paths send consistent ISO timestamps and\n`has_exact_times` on create *and* update. Duration-only entries anchor to local\nnoon of the chosen day (never rolling into the previous day); the date field is\nhidden when exact times are used; default dates are local, not `toISOString()`.\nRemoved the `tt.projects[0]` defaults from the entry form and `TimerWidget`, and\nboth now disable Save/Start plus require an explicit project.\n\nTASK-9: Entries are now editable from the dashboard's recent entries and the\nproject-detail page (the Entries tab already was), all wired to the unified\ncomponent.\n\nTASK-10: Moved `StatisticsView` out of `DashboardView` onto its own\n`?tab=statistics` surface with a sidebar link.\n\nTASK-11: Removed `PomodoroWidget` from the time-tracking dashboard so it no\nlonger competes with the real timer. The component file is left in place,\ncurrently unreferenced — see follow-ups.\n\nTASK-12: Statistics now uses the project's own colour, passes the category\nfilter to the statistics endpoint (`category_ids`) instead of restricting\nprojects client-side, defaults its range in local time, and reports the category\nbar in the shared duration format rather than hours-with-decimals.\n\nTASK-13: Routed sidebar project/category deletes and all entry deletes through\n`ConfirmationModal`, so the same action behaves the same from every surface\n(the detail page already confirmed project deletes).\n\nTASK-14: Removed the hover-only project controls (always visible now), replaced\ndouble-click-to-rename with an explicit pencil button, labelled the colour\npicker, and added `aria-label`s to all icon-only controls. `InlineEditButton`/\n`InlineDeleteButton` gained an optional `label` prop (accessible name) and\n`focus-visible:opacity-100`, without changing other features' behaviour.\n\nTASK-15: Reused `NumberInput`/`DateInput`/`TextInput` across the entry, timer,\nstatistics and project forms, wrapped fields in `<label>` for implicit\nassociation, and replaced silent no-ops with disabled Save buttons (entry,\ntimer, project).\n\nTASK-16: Added `isLightColor`/`getReadableTextColor` to `ColorHelper` (+ tests)\nand used it to guard category-chip/pill contrast; replaced the `#888`/`#9ca3af`\nliterals with theme variables and centralised the category default.\n\nTASK-17: Removed the genuinely unused `timeTracking` keys `duration_minutes`,\n`category`, and `this_month` from all four locales and the shared type.\n\nTASK-18: Used the shared `Heading` for the dashboard title, statistics heading,\nbreakdown-widget title and project-detail title, and spaced the dashboard with a\nconsistent vertical rhythm.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **API contract names are assumed.** `api-brief.md` is not present anywhere in\n  the repo, so the post-change contract was mirrored from the brief's intent:\n  project `color`, update `has_exact_times`, and the statistics filter were named\n  `category_ids` (consistent with the project `category_ids` field). These are\n  all optional/backward-compatible; confirm the real names with the API owner.\n- **`project.total_duration` unit assumed to be minutes** (formatted with the\n  existing `formatDuration`, which takes minutes). Confirm the unit.\n- **Pomodoro (TASK-11) has no home yet.** Per the brief's \"move it out\" option it\n  was removed from the time-tracking dashboard; `PomodoroWidget.svelte` is now\n  unreferenced and awaits a product decision (wire to a real entry vs. relocate).\n- **TASK-17 scope reduction.** `add_category`, `edit_category`, and `color` are\n  now referenced by TASK-14 (the brief allows \"remove *or* wire up\"), and the\n  `welcome_tour.steps.timeTracking` tips are consumed by `WelcomeTour.svelte`\n  (the task's \"orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking`\" does not exist in the repo),\n  so those were kept.\n- **Pre-existing verification failures** (present before this job, unrelated):\n  `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` \"StatisticWidget\" colour-class test\n  fails, and `npm run lint` fails prettier across ~450 untouched files. There are\n  also pre-existing eslint errors in untouched files (e.g. `Calendars.svelte.ts`).\n  `npm run check` is clean and all time-tracking/new tests pass.\n- `node_modules` was absent; `npm ci` was run to restore the pinned dependencies\n  purely to execute the project's own `check`/`test`/`lint` commands. No\n  dependency was added or changed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":121,"totalLines":121,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/joke_time-tracking-improvements/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791628358306,"end":1791628358309}},"id":"prt_1255f3269001vSPh1AF5I9uRkN","sessionID":"ses_edaa0f8d5ffeDEZMADxwKw1010","messageID":"msg_1255f2cc80014amDAUTKD6bYYG"}}
